docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-514-
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md:515:## A1.7 The agreement gate, hardened
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-516-
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-517-The original gate asked author and AI to independently *agree* the model is
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-518-faithful. Confirmation tasks produce weak evidence: a reviewer re-reads the
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-519-author's framing and nods, because the framing is persuasive — that is why
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-520-the author chose it. And the AI collaborator that helped author the model
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-521-agreeing with it is close to self-review. Two changes, both consistent with
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-522-§4.5's different-model discipline, applied one level up:
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-523-
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-524-1. **The fidelity review is a falsification task performed by non-author
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-525-   models.** Models that had no hand in authoring the formal model receive
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-526-   the A1.2 property list (prose) and the model itself, and are tasked
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-527-   adversarially: *construct a concrete trace the model accepts that the
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-528-   properties say must be rejected, or a property the prose implies that
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-529-   the model fails to state.* A reviewer who hunted for a counterexample
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-530-   and failed is evidence; a reviewer who agreed is a nod. The hunt's
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-531-   artifacts are committed either way — found or not found — and each
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-532-   review records, for reproducibility: model, vendor, and date; the
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-533-   prompts used; configuration where available; the hash of the exact
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-534-   input bundle; and whether the reviewer saw prior review transcripts.
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-535-
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-536-2. **Model-derived conformance vectors.** The model checker's explored
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-537-   traces are mechanically extracted into concrete fixtures for the real
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-538-   verifier — each trace names inputs and the verdict the model requires
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-539-   (e.g., "manifest requires {KMS, GPG}, bundle carries only KMS →
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-540-   `INVALID`"). This narrows the declared model-to-code gap (the code is
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-541-   tested against the model's exact predictions, not hand-written
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-542-   approximations of them) and doubles as a fidelity check: an unfaithful
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-543-   model, concretized into fixtures, produces *visibly absurd test cases*
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-544-   — far easier to catch than a subtle misstatement in temporal logic.
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-545-   These vectors become part of the H1a suite, with a clean division of
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-546-   labor: model-derived vectors *evidence* conformance to the model on the
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-547-   extracted traces — testing, not proof of implementation/model
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-548-   equivalence, preserving the original's attested-not-proven discipline
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-549-   for the model-to-code gap; the adversarially-authored red-bar attacks
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-550-   (§4.5) hunt for what is *outside* the model. **Declared limitation:** the trace-to-fixture translation
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-551-   is itself a step with fidelity risk — abstract states must be
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-552-   concretized into real byte-level bundles. The concretizer is therefore
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-553-   reviewed under the same non-author discipline, and its output is
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-554-   spot-audited by eye; the risk is named, not waved off.
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-555-
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-556-**Declared residual risk — self-adjudication.** Whether a reviewer's
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-557-counterexample stands or is refuted is judged by the author. Independent
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-558-adjudication costs money the pre-registered no-spend constraint (H3)
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-559-forbids; the softness is therefore declared rather than concealed, and
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-560-every adjudication (counterexample accepted or refuted, with reasoning) is
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-561-committed alongside the review artifacts, so a future reader can re-judge.
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-562-
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-563-H0's resolution criteria are amended accordingly: requirement (2) now
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-564-reads — the falsification-task review by non-author models has run, its
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-565-artifacts are committed, and no unrefuted counterexample stands; and the
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md-566-conformance-vector extraction is added to the H1a evidence obligations.
