docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-110-## A9.1 V1's success definition, claim, profile and scenario mapping — OWNER DECISION (Q1), implementing A and C
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-111-
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-112-**Success definition** (`docs/V1-SCHEDULE.md`, adopted here). V1 succeeds when:
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-113-1. An organisation can obtain a receipt, at a stated cost and latency, asserting that *these exact bytes were
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-114-   presented, signed by key K whose authority is evidenced by named channels, no later than time T*.
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-115-2. A relying party can verify that claim without Tessera running and without the authors' help. From V1's
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-116-   documentation alone, it reaches the safe decision on every case of the registered mapping below, including the
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-117-   cases whose answer is "not established": **zero unsafe accepts; false rejects only on d2 and h** (AUTHOR
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-118-   DECISION C; this replaces V1-SCHEDULE's "the prototype's scenario set"). *Evidence:* one human tester (n = 1,
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-119-   recorded under the pseudonym "Aki Doe") who meets the independence criteria of `docs/V1-TESTER-BRIEF.md`: a CS
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-120-   background; no knowledge of attestation, timestamping, blockchains or this project; has not discussed Tessera
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-121-   with the author; and no help from the project during the test. The evidence is stated as one tester's result,
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-122-   not as a result about relying parties in general.
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-123-3. V1 ships by 4 December 2026, or the project stops pursuing V1 by explicit decision at that point.
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-124-
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-125-Milestones (ceilings, accepted by the author 2026-10-09: *"I'll accept those dates"*): 16 Oct, 30 Oct, 20 Nov,
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-126-4 Dec, with V1-SCHEDULE's slip rule.
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-127-
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-128-**Claim.** *Conditional on the registered cryptographic and key-use assumptions, a V1 receipt lets anyone holding it
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-129-establish, without Tessera, that the attested content was presented to the Tessera V1 service, whose own domain is
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-130-D; that each of the service's two keys K = {K_kms, K_gpg} signed its own frame binding that content; that two named
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-131-channels authenticated these keys for D, with an issuance window the git channel committed, in chain order, before
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-132-the receipt's anchor, at the stated evidence times; that
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-133-the signed frames and their exact signatures existed no later than T; and that the declared issue time is not
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-134-earlier than the window's not-before and the verified chain-time T is not later than its not-after. Effective
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-135-revocation and historical algorithm and key safety are not evaluated, and the receipt attests neither the
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-136-submitter nor the content's meaning. The verdict is typed and says what was not established.*
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-137-
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-138-| # | Sub-claim | Non-claim kept beside it |
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-139-|---|---|---|
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-140-| C1 Bytes | The verifier reconstructs each signer's exact frame; both bind the same content and common metadata, the designated fingerprint in its slot. The receipt-anchor preimage `A_sig` over both frames and both signatures is unambiguous. | Nothing about meaning or truth. Payload identity is not frame equality. |
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-141-| C2 Presentation | The content was presented at some issuance event of the V1 service (existential). | Not who submitted it; not whether a replay suits the transaction. |
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-142-| C3 Signature | Each required signature verifies over its designated frame; a missing, stripped or substituted one fails. | **The two keys are separate technical failure domains under a single controller; V1 claims no separation of control and no independent fates**, and no independent approval of content. The `gpg` signer signs frames delivered by the AWS-side issuer, so capture of the issuing account confers signing capability for both slots; the non-exportable key prevents key export, not misuse. |
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-143-| C4 Authority | DNSSEC (owner name D, evaluated at the snapshot's own anchored time) and the anchored git key assertion (full commit→tree→blob path) authenticated K for D, with the issuance window, at their evidence times. **Chain-order pre-commitment** (OWNER DECISION 2026-10-14, BROADEN; `docs/reviews/spec-sufficiency/` F01): the git assertion's selected anchor height plus 5 is lower than the receipt's selected anchor height, so the window was confirmed at k = 6 in the chain before the receipt was anchored. The verifier fixes the required set. | Revocation not evaluated. Not public publication of the commit. Neither channel commits to any receipt (CODEX-REVIEW 3). Pre-commitment is chain order, not UTC (A2.1); DNSSEC evidence establishes no publication before issue. |
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-144-| C5 Time | The frames **and their exact signatures** existed no later than T, the verified attestation at the lowest block height in the presented OTS proof (both T and its confirmations come from that attestation; OWNER DECISION 2026-10-14, F03: header times are not monotone, so "earliest" means chain order); the three-conjunct predicate holds at k = 6. | Presentation-sensitive T. No lower bound, no priority. Header times are chain-time proxies. Reorganization deeper than k is a residual. |
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-145-| C6 Without Tessera | The verdict is a pure function of the bundle, the published verifier and its distributed trust configuration. | Custody is the holder's. Dead-project reconstruction not demonstrated. A selected anchor (C5) beyond the newest pin is `UNVERIFIABLE`. Every supplied header must be pinned. An unselected attestation without its headers supplies no fact and is not a failure (OWNER DECISION 2026-10-14, F02). |
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md:146:| C7 Safe decision | The verdict is typed and reports `revocation: NOT_EVALUATED`, `historical_security: NOT_EVALUATED` and standing separately; a non-expert makes no unsafe accept on the mapping (4 Dec criterion, not yet established). Assigned build evidence includes A9.4's missing-capture negative control. | Revocation, historical security and standing are not claimed. |
