docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-407-**Issuance window.** The key-publication record carries `issuance-not-before` and `issuance-not-after`, **both
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-408-mandatory**, identical in DNS and the git blob (ENCODING-V1 §7, §7.1, D-17).
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-409-- **Registered invariant: `issuance-not-after − issuance-not-before ≤ 90 days`** (a record that violates it is
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-410-  rejected, `DNS_WINDOW_LENGTH`). This amendment registers the first issuance window only; it does not yet
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-411-  authorize successor issuance. A future sequential-replacement registration may retain the frozen V1 byte/check
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-412-  profile: the same DNS owner and git path, new keys, and a new window with next.not-before > previous.not-after (both
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-413-  endpoints are inclusive). Each receipt carries its own historical snapshot and commit. Multiple TXT records at the
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-414-  required owner fail `DNS_RRSET`; a substituted per-key owner name fails `DNS_OWNER`. The V1 verifier checks each
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-415-  receipt's window, not non-overlap between receipts. Before successor issuance, the owner records a dated rotation
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-416-  registration naming the two-window positive/negative vectors and the model, checked property and result
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-417-  establishing the intended issuance invariant. This future rotation evidence is not added to the 30 Oct
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-418-  first-window gate. Without that registration, issuance stops at the first window's end.
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-419-- **Verifier rule (C4).** A receipt is `INVALID / ISSUANCE_WINDOW` unless the declared issue time is not earlier
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-420-  than not-before and the verified chain-time T is not later than not-after, with T as registered and no margin.
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-421-  T itself is not compared with not-before.
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-422-- **Issuer invariant.** An attempt whose T would exceed not-after is not shipped. The stop margin, the window's
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-423-  actual dates and the rotation plan are operating numbers, not registered (`docs/V1-OPERATIONS-RUNBOOK.md`).
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-424-- A published window cannot be shortened; detection changes no V1 verdict.
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-425-- The relying-party documentation states: `ISSUANCE_WINDOW` can result from presenting a later proof; ask the
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-426-  holder for the issuer's original proof.
