docs/V1-PROFILE.md-273-### 3.3 Precedence and verdicts
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-274-
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-275-- Order of decision: any required check failed gives `INVALID`; else any required check unperformable gives
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-276-  `UNVERIFIABLE`; else `VALID_STRICT`. There is no waiver set, so the degraded branch never applies. [SPEC
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-277-  R-5.25:1368; A9:161]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-278-- `INVALID` dominates `UNVERIFIABLE`. [A9:182; SPEC R-5.26:1370; SPEC R-2.33:300] Case d3 depends on it.
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-279-- The unperformable rule applies to required checks only. [SPEC R-2.32:298]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-280-- A verdict is never a bare boolean. `UNVERIFIABLE` is never promoted. [SPEC R-2.34:302; SPEC R-5.38:1394]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-281-- No fallback, negotiation or normalization during verification. [SPEC R-5.18:1266; ENC §1.2:156-158]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-282-- **Aggregation.** Physical evaluation order is unrestricted, but reporting uses the fixed total check order (section
docs/V1-PROFILE.md:283:  15.7). Early termination is permitted only when every earlier-priority reportable check is settled and every
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-284-  stable field, including T, is determined. A failure prevents only checks whose own necessary input cannot be
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-285-  obtained; it does not suppress independent receipt-anchor evaluation needed for T. Derived checks are unperformable
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-286-  when necessary inputs cannot be obtained, and never pass by default. ~~An unknown `alg` routes the slot as opaque
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-287-  (Lemma 7a)~~: signature and possession semantics under an `alg` other than the catalog-supported id are
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-288-  unperformable; independent schema and hash checks still run. Codec routing is section 1's codec-known versus
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-289-  policy-supported rule. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G26; r2-F01] *Dated correction 2026-10-14: the resolutions draft's "a
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-290-  verifier may stop early only on a failed check" is withdrawn; it let two schedules report different stable
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-291-  fields. Dated correction 2026-10-14 (r2-F01): "an unknown `alg` routes the slot as opaque" is withdrawn; it
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-292-  conflicted with ENC's codec selection for a codec-known but unselected id.*
