docs/V1-PROFILE.md-334-
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-335-**Interface convention, not a verdict rule.** This subsection records how the conformance suite and the
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-336-differential harness drive a verifier under test. It changes no verdict, reason or T, binds no production release,
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-337-and gives way to the release artefact and release-signature format when those are decided (section 14.2 items 1,
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-338-2). Both implementations of differential run 1 used it. [OWNER 2026-10-14, interface convention from diff-1,
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-339-EA-01/EA-02/EA-03/EA-12] *The release format is now section 15.9. The TEST provisioning below is an instrument
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-340-interface only: it is never a release, and an installed production verifier refuses it (section 15.9 R4).*
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-341-[OWNER 2026-10-19, §14.2 item 2, `docs/V1-FREEZE-OPEN.md` §3]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-342-- **Invocation and compiled-in inputs (EA-01).** `CMD --trust <config> --bundle <bundle>`. The compiled-in trust
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-343-  configuration hash and catalog (section 1, section 5) are provisioned for TEST by environment: the TEST release
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-344-  record from `TESSERA_V1_TEST_RELEASE`, authenticated by the public key in `TESSERA_V1_TEST_RELEASE_KEY`, and the
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-345-  catalog from `TESSERA_V1_TEST_CATALOG`. A config whose hash is not the one compiled by an authentically signed
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-346-  release is refused (`TRUST_CONFIG_UNAUTHENTICATED`, no verdict).
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-347-- **Request (EA-02).** The request (D4) is `strict` by default; `--request <value>` supplies any other value.
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-348-- **Output and refusal (EA-03).** A verdict is one JSON object on stdout carrying the six stable fields, either at
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-349-  top level or under `stable`, `result` or `report`; diagnostics may accompany it. *Instrument convention
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-350-  [OWNER 2026-10-19, A10.1.1]:* the independent verifier prints `{"stable":<stable-output object>,
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-351-  "utc_assessment":<section 7.4 object>}`; the conformance runner compares `utc_assessment` only where a case's
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-352-  `expected.json` carries one. A startup refusal is a nonzero
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-353-  exit with the refusal code on stdout or stderr and no six-field object.
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-354-- **Release checker (EA-12).** `CMD --previous <config> --next <config>` prints `ACCEPT` or `REJECT` for the release
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-355-  invariants of section 5.
