docs/V1-PROFILE.md-446-- **Root KSKs, three periods each.** The trust configuration records each KSK's signing and reliance periods
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-447-  separately from its publication and revocation dates. [A9:154-155; A9:324-325] The instrument spike found that
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-448-  conflating signing with publication falsely rejected every snapshot from 2026-10-11. [SR:73-78]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-449-- **Root rule.** The root DNSKEY set is valid at the snapshot's anchored time if some trusted KSK whose **reliance
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-450-  period** contains that time validates it. Each KSK entry records signing-start, signing-end and a sourced reliance lifetime L; the reliance
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-451-  interval is [signing-start, signing-end + L]. L is an acceptance-policy value from cited RRSIG validity evidence,
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-452-  labelled observed, not a proven global maximum. The extension admits authentic pre-retirement evidence anchored
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-453-  later and does not prove signing before retirement: a thief of a retired KSK can manufacture eligible evidence
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-454-  during it (A9.5; AUTHOR ADOPTED 2026-10-13, kind CORRECT). *Dated correction 2026-10-13: the earlier wording
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-455-  ("maximum validity … it made"; "usable for that long and no longer") overclaimed provenance and is withdrawn.* The rule is existential and
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-456-  order-independent: a candidate that fails is informational, and the result is computed once, after every eligible
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-457-  key has been tried. A trusted KSK that is published but did not sign is informational, never a failure.
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-458-  [A9.5, A9:309-325, OWNER DECISION 2026-10-13 after `docs/reviews/v1-profile/` F1, F2]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-459-- **Rollover control (required vector).** A snapshot taken while one trusted KSK is published but not signing must
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-460-  pass. [A9:341-342] Further required vectors (`docs/reviews/v1-profile/` F1, F2 dispositions): a failing trusted
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-461-  candidate listed before a validating one, in both trust-list orders, must pass; an honest old root signed before
