docs/V1-PROFILE.md-638-- Owner name is `_tessera-v1.<D>`. The verifier rebuilds it from the signed `issuer` and compares label by label,
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-639-  ignoring ASCII case. Anything else is `DNS_OWNER`. [ENC §7:551-556] This is the owner-name check (G-21 / M2).
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-640-- One TXT RRset, one RR, one character-string. The value grammar, the fifteen-step rejection order and the
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-641-  exact-255-byte rule are in ENC §7. [ENC §7:557-612]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-642-- The record carries `kms`, `gpg`, `profile`, `issuance-not-before` and `issuance-not-after`, all mandatory, in a
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-643-  fixed order. [ENC §7:569-579]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-644-- The DNSSEC chain is validated against the root rule (section 5) at the snapshot's own anchored time (section 7.3).
