docs/V1-PROFILE.md-646-- **Root rule first.** The root RRset passes only under A9.5: a byte-matching configured KSK, usable in its reliance
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-647-  interval at T_snap, verifies a selected RRSIG valid at T_snap. The algorithm profile below never replaces that
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-648-  eligibility condition. Candidate aggregation is existential and order-independent; extra candidates are
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-649-  informational after any eligible supported path passes. Root outcomes and their precedence are section 5's.
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-650-  [OWNER 2026-10-14, G16]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-651-- **Supported DNSSEC set (NARROW-CLAIM, visible owner scope choice).** DNSKEY and RRSIG algorithms 8 (RSA/SHA-256,
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-652-  RFC 5702, key per RFC 3110) and 13 (ECDSA P-256/SHA-256, RFC 6605); DS digest types 2 (SHA-256, RFC 4509) and 4
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-653-  (SHA-384, RFC 6605). The DNSKEY used has the Zone Key flag set, REVOKE clear, protocol 3. Validation is RFC 4035
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-654-  §5.3.1–5.3.3 at T_snap with RFC 4034 §6 canonical form. DS is signed by a key in the parent's validated DNSKEY
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-655-  set; a child DNSKEY RRset is self-signed by a key matching a validated DS; the TXT is signed by a key in its zone's
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-656-  validated DNSKEY set. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G16]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-657-- **Outcomes for each non-root required RRset**, computed once after every candidate is tried [OWNER 2026-10-14,
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-658-  G16]:
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-659-  1. some supported path (matching authenticated DS → DNSKEY → RRSIG) validates at T_snap: pass;
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-660-  2. else the RRset or the witness RRSIG it needs is missing: `UNVERIFIABLE / DNS_EVIDENCE_MISSING`;
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-661-  3. else an unsupported algorithm or digest type could supply the path: `UNVERIFIABLE /
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-662-     DNSSEC_ALGORITHM_UNSUPPORTED`;
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-663-  4. else (every possibility supported and checked) a candidate verifies but its window excludes T_snap, or its
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-664-     times are edge failures (section 7.3): `INVALID / RRSIG_NOT_VALID_AT_EVAL_TIME` (or that edge reason);
