docs/V1-PROFILE.md-723-### 6.2 Issuance window (C4 verifier rule)
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-724-
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-725-- The window `issuance-not-after − issuance-not-before` is at most 90 days. A record that violates it is rejected
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-726-  (`DNS_WINDOW_LENGTH`). V1 has one window and no overlap. [A9:409-411; ENC §7:578-580]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-727-- A receipt is `INVALID / ISSUANCE_WINDOW` unless `issuance-not-before` ≤ declared issue time and T ≤
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-728-  `issuance-not-after`. Both bounds are inclusive. T is compared as registered, with no margin. T is not compared
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-729-  with not-before. [A9:419-421; ENC §7.1:636-643, 662-663]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-730-- The guarantee is in chain time. A UTC cutoff would need a backward-skew bound V1 does not establish. [A9:441-447;
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-731-  ENC §7.1:661-671]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-732-- A published window cannot be shortened. [A9:424]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-733-- The window, its dates and the stop margin are operating facts, not profile rules. [A9:422-423; RB §2]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-734-
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-735-### 6.3 Git channel
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-736-
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-737-The OTS stamp targets the signed commit's object id, never a tree, blob or unsigned commit. [A9:297-299; ENC
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-738-§7.2:685-691] The verifier does four things:
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-739-
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-740-1. Recomputes the commit id from the presented raw commit object.
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-741-2. Verifies `gpgsig` over the object without that header, under the pinned repository key.
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-742-3. Follows commit, then tree, then blob, down the fixed path below.
--
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-841-- **Receipt consistency, explicit** [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F02]: "Both frames' signer fingerprints equal the
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-842-  corresponding manifest fingerprints (RECEIPT_SLOT); their common byte substrings are equal
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-843-  (RECEIPT_COMMON_MISMATCH); common issuer and alg equal manifest issuer and alg (RECEIPT_MANIFEST_MISMATCH). Stage 4
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-844-  checks common.manifest_sha256 against SHA256(F_manifest), using RECEIPT_MANIFEST_MISMATCH; when both common objects
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-845-  are available, check each in kms/gpg order. These checks never require signature validity or channel
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-846-  authentication." All are `INVALID`. Anchor digest verification stays in the receipt OTS check; with the
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-847-  `a_sig`-only route there is no second externally transported tuple to reconcile. A9's bytes/signature binding
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-848-  remains required; this completes the specification and permits omitting none of these checks. Listed in section
docs/V1-PROFILE.md:849:  15.7 (rows 4 and 6).
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-850-- **W1 (malleability).** Decided. No V1 semantic, standing or attempt identifier is derived from signature bytes. The
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-851-  anchor digest commits to them by design and is not an identifier. V1 does not require unique signatures and
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-852-  normalizes none. The unhashed OpenPGP area carries no meaning. A changed signature fails the anchor
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-853-  (`RECEIPT_ANCHOR_MISMATCH`). [ENC §3.5:339-355; ENC §8:735-739; A9:295-296] The half-day argument that no strict
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-854-  query relies on signature uniqueness is a separate item (DD:89; step 10).
