docs/V1-PROFILE.md-856-## 7. Time
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-857-
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-858-### 7.1 The T rule
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-859-
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-860-- T is the time of the verified attestation at the **lowest block height** in the presented OTS proof; both T and
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-861-  its confirmations come from that attestation. It is presentation-sensitive: a different presentation of the same
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-862-  receipt can select a different T. [A9 C5 as revised 2026-10-14; DD:56, 98-99; OWNER 2026-10-14, G03] *Dated
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-863-  correction 2026-10-14: this bullet previously read "T is the time of the earliest verified attestation", A9's
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-864-  earlier wording. "Earliest" means chain order, not least nTime: header times are not monotone, and the two
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-865-  selection rules can give different verdicts on the same proof.*
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-866-- No lower bound and no priority. Header times are chain-time proxies. [A9:144]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-867-- The three conjuncts at k = 6 (`DepthK = k − 1 = 5`): `declared − ε ≤ anchor_time`; `anchor_time ≤ declared + δ`;
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-868-  `confirmed_at ≤ declared + δ`. All three are evaluated together. [SPEC R-4.41:985; SPEC R-5.19:1352; SPEC
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-869-  V33-V36:1342-1346; A9:105-106]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-870-- A real proof carries several attestations hours apart and nothing in the proof names T (M3). [FT:20; DD:98]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-871-- **T ≡ `anchor_time`.** For the receipt proof, T = `anchor_time` = nTime(h*), where h* is the lowest qualifying
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-872-  height. The same value feeds conjuncts 1 and 2, the C4 window rule and the reported T. Two qualifying attestations
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-873-  at the same height give the same T. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G03] *(Was: "`OPEN (step 8):` one sentence stating whether
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-874-  T is the `anchor_time` of the three conjuncts", 2026-10-13.)*
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-875-- **`confirmed_at`** = nTime(h* + 5): the including block plus five successors, k = 6 (SPEC R-3.45, R-4.42). A
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-876-  failure gives `INVALID`: `TIME_BEFORE_DECLARED_EPSILON`, `TIME_AFTER_DECLARED_DELTA` or `CONFIRMATION_LATE`.
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-877-  Nonmonotone header times can give `confirmed_at` < T; that is not a failure, and there is no monotonicity check.
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-878-  [OWNER 2026-10-14, G04]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-879-- **Qualifying ("verified") attestation.** A Bitcoin attestation at height h qualifies if and only if (a) the
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-880-  bundled header at h exists and its merkle root equals the attestation message; (b) headers h … h+5 are all
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-881-  bundled; (c) each equals its pin, `hex(reverse(SHA256d(header))) = pin[height]`; (d) for i = h+1 … h+5,
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-882-  `header_i.prev = SHA256d(header_{i−1})`. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G05] *(Was: "`OPEN (step 8):` what 'verified' means
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-883-  for an attestation", 2026-10-13.)*
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-884-- **Selection.** Attestation selection is existential over qualifying branches. A syntactically valid Bitcoin
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-885-  attestation without a complete h..h+5 segment is nonqualifying, not a required failed check. It supplies no time or
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-886-  trust fact. All supplied headers, including unused ones, are independently checked against pins (section 7.2).
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-887-  The selected anchor, rather than every unverified attestation, is the referent of "anchors beyond the newest pin"
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-888-  (A9 C6 as revised 2026-10-14). [OWNER 2026-10-14, G05]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-889-- **Proof outcomes.** A pinned bundled header at h whose merkle root ≠ the attestation message: `INVALID /
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-890-  OTS_MERKLE_MISMATCH` (a contradicted branch fails the proof). No qualifying attestation: `UNVERIFIABLE /
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-891-  HEADERS_MISSING` if any Bitcoin attestation is present, `UNVERIFIABLE / ANCHOR_PENDING_ONLY` if only pending ones;
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-892-  the snapshot uses `SNAPSHOT_NOT_ANCHORED` and git `GIT_NOT_ANCHORED`. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G05]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-893-- **Time arithmetic.** Times are integer seconds since 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z without leap seconds; nTime is the
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-894-  header's uint32; RFC 3339 fields convert by days-from-civil (proleptic Gregorian); comparisons are inclusive.
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-895-  [OWNER 2026-10-14, G03]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-896-- **OTS and txid encoding**: section 15.2. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G20]
