docs/V1-PROFILE.md-898-  txid-equality check applies only to receipt_anchor. The snapshot/git proofs use the closed OTS grammar and header
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-899-  qualification, with no txid comparison. Select h* before the receipt txid check; any satisfying qualifying path at
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-900-  exactly h* passes that check. Never switch to a higher height merely to find a matching txid." **Owner choice
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-901-  (fail-closed), stated separately:** the **transaction-shape and merkle-suffix subset** (section 15.2, parts 1, 2
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-902-  and 4, without part 3's txid comparison) also applies to the selected height of the snapshot and git proofs; a
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-903-  failure there is `INVALID / OTS_TX_SHAPE`, and any qualifying path at exactly that proof's h* satisfying the
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-904-  subset passes. No receipt txid is compared with the snapshot or git proof; the three proofs normally anchor in
