docs/V1-PROFILE.md-908-### 7.2 Header pins
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-909-
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-910-- Every bundle header must be in the pinned set. Otherwise the verdict is `UNVERIFIABLE / HEADERS_NOT_COVERED`.
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-911-  There is no retarget logic, because the pins cover every accepted header. [A9:156; DD:99]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-912-- **Conflict.** A supplied header at a pinned height with a different hash gives `INVALID / HEADER_CONFLICTS_PIN`:
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-913-  it is contradictory evidence. A9.1's "a bundle header outside the pins" is read as a header **at a height the pins
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-914-  do not cover**. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G23] A10.5 stage 1 (signed 2026-10-18) registers this reading as A9's meaning:
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-915-  no pin at the height gives `UNVERIFIABLE / HEADERS_NOT_COVERED`, a header differing from its pin gives `INVALID /
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-916-  HEADER_CONFLICTS_PIN`. [OWNER 2026-10-19, Levadura contested 2] *(Was: "`OPEN (step 8):` the verdict for a header that … conflicts with a
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-917-  pin", 2026-10-13.)*
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-918-- **Coverage.** Required: headers h* … h*+5 of the selected attestation of each of the three proofs (receipt,
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-919-  snapshot, git), all in the shared `headers` pool. Every supplied header, used or not, is checked against the pins.
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-920-  A `headers` entry that fails row 2.4 is not a supplied header: it contributes `CONTAINER_SCHEMA` only, and rows
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-921-  10.x, 11.x, 13.4 and 14.6 use the remaining entries [OWNER 2026-10-14, diff-1 F-3].
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-922-  For each pair of supplied headers at consecutive heights, a prev-hash mismatch gives `INVALID /
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-923-  HEADER_CHAIN_BROKEN`; a missing intermediate height is not a broken link. No PoW, nBits or retarget check: a hash
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-924-  equal to a pin implies all of it. At an unselected height, a pinned header with missing successors is ignored,
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-925-  while an unpinned header blocks the bundle (`HEADERS_NOT_COVERED`). [OWNER 2026-10-14, G07, G05] *(Was: "`OPEN
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-926-  (step 8):` which heights the pins must cover for a given proof", 2026-10-13.)*
