docs/V1-PROFILE.md-928-### 7.3 The DNSSEC snapshot rule
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-929-
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-930-- The issuer anchors the DNSSEC snapshot with its own OTS proof. The envelope is ENC §6 under the tag
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-931-  `tessera-v1/dnssec-snapshot`. [DD:94; ENC §6:536-542]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-932-- The verifier checks that the snapshot's anchored time lies inside every RRSIG window in the chain and within
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-933-  [declared − ε, declared + δ]. The issuer re-captures before shipping if it does not. [DD:94] This is an owner
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-934-  decision carried in, not routed. [A9:104-106]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-935-  - "declared" is the receipt's signed `declared_issue_time`, not the snapshot's capture time. Capture-to-anchor
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-936-    latency is a separate observation, not this predicate. (`docs/reviews/v1-profile/` F6, accepted 2026-10-13.)
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-937-  - "every RRSIG window in the chain" means the one witness signature selected to authenticate each required RRset,
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-938-    not every signature offered: an extra expired or invalid signature beside a valid one neither fails the RRset
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-939-    nor narrows the joint window. The instrument's selection order is (key tag, inception, expiration, signature
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-940-    bytes), first that validates. (`docs/reviews/v1-profile/` F5, accepted 2026-10-13.) Exception: an RRSIG
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-941-    with fewer Labels than its owner fails the body restriction wherever it appears (section 6.1).
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-942-    [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F07]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-943-  - **Frozen witness rule.** The selected witness is the **first eligible validating** candidate in (key tag,
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-944-    inception, expiration, signature bytes, canonical RRSIG RDATA, canonical key RDATA) order. For the root, reliance
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-945-    eligibility precedes selection. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G35] *(Previously described only as the instrument's order.)*
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-946-  - Conjunct 3 (`confirmed_at` of the snapshot ≤ declared + δ) is a new owner acceptance restriction, fail-closed. A
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-947-    failure of any conjunct gives `INVALID / SNAPSHOT_TIME`. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G06]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-948-- The chain is evaluated at the snapshot's anchored time, not at T of the receipt. [A9:143]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-949-- Why: the joint RRSIG window measured 1.6 days, shorter than δ (M8). [DD:93]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-950-- **Snapshot body.** A fixed-order sequence of uncompressed RFC 1035 wire RRs in RFC 4034 §6.2 canonical form,
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-951-  section 15.3. Framing violations are `INVALID / SNAPSHOT_FORMAT`; a syntactically complete body lacking a required
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-952-  RRset or its witness RRSIG is `UNVERIFIABLE / DNS_EVIDENCE_MISSING` (root: `NO_TRUSTED_KSK_USABLE`). The conversion
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-953-  from resolver messages happens before stamping and changes S, so each snapshot needs a fresh stamp; earlier
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-954-  stamped JSON snapshots cannot be reused. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G19] *(Was: "`OPEN (step 8):` the snapshot body
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-955-  format", 2026-10-13.)*
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-956-- **Snapshot time.** T_snap = T of the snapshot's own proof under the section 7.1 rule, at the same depth k = 6, and
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-957-  `confirmed_at`(snapshot) likewise. DNSSEC is evaluated at T_snap only; no capture time, receipt T or wall clock is
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-958-  ever used. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G06] *(Was: "`OPEN (step 8):` how the snapshot's anchored time is derived",
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-959-  2026-10-13.)*
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-960-- **RRSIG time arithmetic.** Inception and expiration are 32-bit values v, each resolved to the unique absolute
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-961-  second t with t ≡ v (mod 2^32) and |t − T_snap| < 2^31 (RFC 4034 §3.1.5, RFC 1982). If v − T_snap ≡ 2^31 (mod 2^32)
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-962-  the candidate fails with `RRSIG_TIME_AMBIGUOUS`; if resolved inception > expiration it fails with
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-963-  `RRSIG_INTERVAL_REVERSED`; inception = expiration is allowed. These are candidate failures under the existential
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-964-  rule, ranked with `RRSIG_NOT_VALID_AT_EVAL_TIME`. The witness check is inception ≤ T_snap ≤ expiration, never "now",
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-965-  including in 2106. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G27]
