docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1503-### 15.1 Container [OWNER 2026-10-14, G14, G17, G33]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1504-
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1505-A bundle is one UTF-8 JSON text that passes ENC §1.4 checks 1–5 and 7 and is canonical JCS. It contains no JSON
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1506-numbers. Heights and durations are decimal strings matching `0|[1-9][0-9]*` with value at most 4294967295. Binary
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1507-values are RFC 4648 §4 base64 with padding that round-trips (no non-zero pad bits, no line breaks). Size cap 2^27
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1508-bytes. Top level: exactly `{"layers":[L],"profile":"tessera-v1-strict"}`. After dispatch (section 3.1): a
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1509-non-canonical container is `INVALID / JSON_NONCANONICAL`; then the absence rule (section 2.1) and A9.5's
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1510-`git.object_format` outcomes; then any other schema failure is `INVALID / CONTAINER_SCHEMA`. Absence is inspected
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1511-only beneath correctly typed parents, a present non-string `object_format` is `CONTAINER_SCHEMA`, and a present
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1512-`issuer_record` with an absent internal field is `CONTAINER_SCHEMA` (section 2.1). [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F03]
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1513-
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1514-**Numbers.** JSON numbers are admitted syntactically at dispatch (D1's strict-JSON checks do not exclude them, and
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1515-D2/D3 read only `profile` and the length of `layers`) and rejected after dispatch by the container schema: a JSON
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1516-number anywhere in the layer is `INVALID / CONTAINER_SCHEMA` (row 2.4, after row 2.1), never `OUT_OF_PROFILE`.
