docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1535-
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1536-OWNER CHOICE (supported-path limit). python-opentimestamps 0.4.5 is the reference reader, not normative.
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1537-- **Header.** Magic `00 4f70656e54696d657374616d7073 0000 50726f6f66 00 bf89e2e884e89294`, varuint major version 1,
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1538-  file-hash op `08` (SHA-256 only), the 32-byte digest, one Timestamp, end of input.
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1539-- **Timestamp.** `Timestamp := (ff Item)* Item`; `Item := 00 Attestation | Op Timestamp`.
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1540-- **Ops.** `08` (sha256), `f0 varbytes` (append), `f1 varbytes` (prepend). Arguments 1–4096 bytes; every message and
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1541-  result at most 4096 bytes.
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1542-- **Attestations.** `tag(8) varbytes(payload)`, payload at most 8192 bytes. Bitcoin `0588960d73d71901`: payload is
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1543-  exactly one varuint height. Pending `83dfe30d2ef90c8e`: payload varbytes(URI ≤ 1000), URI ignored.
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1544-- **Wire completion** [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F09]. `varbytes := varuint byte_count || exactly byte_count octets`.
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1545-  Both the pending and the Bitcoin payloads must be consumed exactly (the pending payload's inner URI framing
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1546-  included); otherwise `OTS_FORMAT`. A Bitcoin attestation whose message is not exactly 32 bytes is `INVALID /
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1547-  OTS_FORMAT`, independently of header availability. Timestamp depth: the root Timestamp has depth 0, each Op →
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1548-  Timestamp step adds 1, `ff` siblings do not add. Op and attestation counts are of serialized items, duplicates
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1549-  included; duplicates are semantically inert only within those limits.
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1550-- **Varuint.** LEB128, shortest form only, value ≤ 2^32 − 1. (python-opentimestamps 0.4.5 accepts redundant groups;
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1551-  V1 does not.)
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1552-- **Bounds.** Depth ≤ 256; ≤ 65536 ops and ≤ 4096 attestations per proof; proof ≤ 2^20 bytes. Duplicate identical
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1553-  branches are permitted and have no effect.
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1554-- **Rejections.** Any other op or tag, or any grammar or bound violation: `INVALID / OTS_FORMAT`. File digest must be
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1555-  SHA256(`A_sig`) for the receipt (`RECEIPT_ANCHOR_MISMATCH`), SHA256 of the ENC §6 envelope for the snapshot
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1556-  (`SNAPSHOT_STAMP_MISMATCH`), SHA256 of `<40-hex commit id>\n` for git (`GIT_STAMP_MISMATCH`).
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1557-- **Merkle link.** A Bitcoin attestation's message is 32 bytes and equals bytes 36–68 of the bundled header at that
