docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1748-**Numbered check table** [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F11; incorporates r2-F02–F10 and r2-F12]. The reported reason is
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1749-the first **failed** row in (row id, tie key) order; if no row failed, the first **unperformable** row. A row whose
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1750-necessary input cannot be obtained because of an earlier row's failure or unperformability is unperformable and
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1751-contributes no reason of its own; the table is ordered so that every such dependency points to an earlier row.
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1752-Rows 11.1–11.4 are evaluated whatever else fails, because they determine T (section 3.4). Slot order is kms, then
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1753-gpg. Candidates are ordered by the G35 tuple (section 7.3), never by their position in a transport array; members
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1754-and missing paths by JCS key order with numeric array indices; heights ascending. The verdict rule (section 3.3) is
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1755-unchanged: INVALID over UNVERIFIABLE, and no early exit before every earlier-priority row and every stable field,
docs/V1-PROFILE.md-1756-including T, is settled.
