   150	|---|---|---|
   151	| L0 | Post-issue edit of a real receipt from the AWS issuer; the service verifier runs with the release trust configuration. No service cooperation. | 34 vectors include L0 (INDEX) |
   152	| L1 | Attacker-held keys and re-signing by the tester | SP1-03/04, SP2-04, E6A-01, P4-04, G10-*, CAP-01 |
   153	| L2 | Authority channels the tester controls: a staging domain, repository and trust configuration, or the TEST universe. **Never the production `wamason.com` channels.** | SP1-03/04, G10-*, CAP-01, P9-03 |
   154	| L3 | Frames signed by the service keys over inputs the tester chooses. Needs the TEST issuer, or a staging-only adversarial hook. | SP1-02, SP2-06 (has an L0 variant: splice two real receipts), CAP-04 |
   155	| L4 | Chosen Bitcoin header times. TEST universe only: synthetic chain and TEST pins. Mainnet cannot produce these. | TMP-01..08, ISS-01/02 |
   156	| L5 | Issuer behaviour under fault injection or a simulated chain/clock | ISS-01..04 |
   157	| L6 | Control of the verifier's environment: network isolation, two hosts, a reachable service that contradicts the bundle | P9-01..03 |
   158	
   159	**What this means for the service:**
   160	
   161	- **Verifier interface.** The service verifier must accept the run.py contract (`prototype/conformance/run.py:6-24`):
   162	  `--trust` and `--bundle`, a request input, and the six stable fields plus `utc_assessment` on stdout. It also needs
   163	  a mode that loads a **TEST release and trust configuration**. Without that mode, the L4 temporal vectors (late
   164	  burial, A3.9, the ε side, the tolerance cases) cannot run against the AWS verifier at all: their header times
   165	  cannot be chosen on mainnet.
   166	- **Issuer test surface.** ISS-01..04 need one on a staging deployment: a header-source stub or simulated chain, a
   167	  calendar fault switch, and a compressible lifecycle clock. Run in real time, ISS-04 would take about 3 × 96 h.
   168	  Through the public API alone, only ISS-03's live half can be observed: any returned receipt must hold
   169	  h*..h*+5 for all three proofs.
   170	- **P9 vectors** test the distributed verifier release, not an API. A verifier behind a network API cannot be the
   171	  system under test for "no network". P9-02 does apply to the API, though: repeat submissions must give the same
   172	  six fields.
   173	- **Real material.** L0 vectors need one or two real receipts. CAP-03 and the L0 variant of SP2-06 need two receipts
   174	  with different content. P7-01 needs a receipt whose content embeds another bundle, issued as an ordinary client
   175	  request.
