docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-10.md:773:| 37 | "**Chain-order pre-commitment** (…): the git assertion's selected anchor height plus 5 is lower than the receipt's selected anchor height" (C4, claim cell) | A9:143 (C4) | Added after it: "The release that first lists the receipt's service-key entry is OpenTimestamps-stamped over its trust-configuration SHA-256, and its selected anchor height plus 5 is lower than the receipt's selected anchor height; otherwise the listing subchecks of A10.4.1 apply (`LISTING_PROOF_MISSING`, `OTS_FORMAT`, `LISTING_STAMP_MISMATCH`, `OTS_MERKLE_MISMATCH`, `HEADERS_MISSING` or `ANCHOR_PENDING_ONLY`, `OTS_TX_SHAPE`, `LISTING_NOT_PRECOMMITTED`), in the order registered there." Non-claim added: "The retrospective protection requires a conforming verifier and independently authenticated Bitcoin history for both selected anchors and their six-header segments. The receipt, listing, snapshot and git proofs must use the same independently authenticated history. For this theft protection, a signature under the possibly stolen release key is not sufficient pin authentication. Compare every used pin with independently validated Bitcoin history, or with a previously retained, independently authenticated genuine release that covers that height. An earlier release with no pin at the height supplies no witness. A party unable to establish this history has not established the retrospective protection. Authenticating only the bootstrap public-key fingerprint does not distinguish a fork signed with the stolen genuine key. An independently retained genuine release/configuration commitment can distinguish such a fork to the extent of its recorded contents and ancestry." (A10.4.1, OWNER DECISION 2026-10-18, narrowed after review r4) Option (e) only. **AUTHOR ADOPTED 2026-10-18** (with option (e); owner decision 2026-10-18, narrowed after review r4) | BROADEN | B |
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-10.md:774:| 38 | "*Trust configuration* (ships with the verifier, never from the bundle)" | A9:154 | Adds to what ships with the verifier, never from the bundle: "an installed, archived listing-evidence package, outside the receipt bundle: for each exact service-key/window tuple, the canonical first-listing configuration, its authenticated release/archive binding and signatures, its completed OTS proof and the raw headers of its selected six-header segment; a release-authenticated manifest mapping each tuple to the first-listing configuration's SHA-256, established by the release checker against the authenticated predecessor chain, with the intervening configurations and authentication/key-transition evidence preserved; and independently authenticated history/pin evidence and the bootstrap record. These are declared verification inputs, hashed in the diagnostics; none is fetched from Tessera during offline verification." (A10.4.1, OWNER DECISION 2026-10-18, narrowed after review r4) Option (e) only. **AUTHOR ADOPTED 2026-10-18** (with option (e); owner decision 2026-10-18, narrowed after review r4) | BROADEN | B |
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-10.md:775:| 39 | "*Issuer invariant:* a receipt ships only when complete; an operator refusal never concerns a shipped receipt." | A9:165 | Adds, after row 29's sentence: "Every verifier release is OpenTimestamps-stamped. Before issuing any receipt in a window, an installed configuration with coverage of the stamp of the release that first lists the exact entry is available, with its listing evidence; for the initial window this is the C0/C1 bootstrap of A10.4.1, and the receipt selects a height strictly greater than h_C0+5." Relying-party text adds: "Preserve the listing-evidence package with the receipt, including the release that first lists the exact entry and its proof. Failure to retain evidence is not evidence of fraud." (A10.4.1, OWNER DECISION 2026-10-18, narrowed after review r4) Option (e) only. **AUTHOR ADOPTED 2026-10-18** (with option (e); owner decision 2026-10-18, narrowed after review r4) | BROADEN | B |
